# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ summary
def summary():
    cnt = collections.Counter(r[4] for r in rows)
    L = []
    L.append('# Claim check 2 (revision 1 of the arXiv draft)\n')
    L.append('Independent claim check of main.tex, sections 00, 01, 03 to 08 and the two model tables. Report only: no draft file and nothing under the ASK-memory-governance repository was edited. Evidence was read from the repository at baseline commit f6bf66e (exported with git archive to /tmp, read only), the Phase 4 to 16 audit record, raw per-call result rows of the decomposition runs (public development items only), and the V12 backup run directory (aggregates only).\n')
    L.append('## Items I could not check, or checked only partly (read first)\n')
    L.append('1. Section 2 (related work), its table and the bibliography beyond key presence were not checked; the claim "each element has prior or concurrent precedent" is therefore UNVERIFIABLE here (CC2-ABS-13, CC2-INT-11).')
    L.append('2. The 60 hidden MGP-6 components, the hidden model inputs, hidden predictions and the per-probe shortcut accuracies are private or not tracked. Hidden-split numbers were taken from the tracked analysis json (artifacts/analysis/mgp6_v43_full_benchmark_analysis.json) and the confusion matrix in it; the cluster bootstrap intervals were not recomputed (the private component map was not opened). Pool structure was recomputed on the 40 public components only (CC2-MGP-09, CC2-MGP-14).')
    L.append('3. The 950 MB LongMemEval slice, answers, predictions and rationales were not opened. Judgment files were read for counts and flags only; no benchmark text is in any output.')
    L.append('4. The request body of the V12 answer calls is not logged, so "seed 0 was sent" rests on the recovered client code and the seed field of the predictions (CC2-LME-08). What the 9Router gateway adds to the Phase 16 requests cannot be tested; the 2,000 token overhead is an estimate by regression-free differencing.')
    L.append('5. The full repository test suite was not run; five test files (34 tests) were. The git reachability of the 17 recovered code blobs and the byte identity of all baseline shard files were taken from Phase 15 (I recomputed the SHA-256 of the six top-level files named in CC2-APP-01 and of b1 to b4 judgments against the earlier run).')
    L.append('6. The raw rows of the Kimi K2.5 and MiMo v2.6 Flash attempts and the error body of the Qwen-family attempt do not exist in the folder (CC2-APP-14, CC2-APP-16).')
    L.append('7. The hidden scoring time is not recorded; the commit time of the final hidden report (2026-07-26T14:39 local) was used as the reference for "after the hidden scoring".')
    L.append('8. Process note: while searching the audit folder for the origin of the figure 117 I printed two lines of the revision-0 summary through a grep, before I had written my own verdict on the grader composition. The verdict CC2-LME-05 was derived from the raw judgment rows (and the .orig pre-adjudication files) and I did not use those lines. The revision-0 report was otherwise read only after the verdicts were formed.')
    L.append('9. No network, API or paid call was made. The only files written are in review_claimcheck2/ and a temporary export of the baseline commit in /tmp/cc2_base.\n')
    L.append('## Counts\n')
    L.append('Rows in CLAIM_CHECK2_REPORT.csv: %d\n' % len(rows))
    L.append('| Verdict | Count |\n|---|---:|')
    for k in ['SUPPORTED', 'WEAKER_THAN_STATED', 'CONTRADICTED', 'UNVERIFIABLE']: L.append('| %s | %d |' % (k, cnt.get(k, 0)))
    L.append('')
    L.append('## Findings that matter most\n')
    L.append('1. **Grader composition (CONTRADICTED, CC2-LME-05).** Before adjudication the 128 correct answers are 118 parsed model-judge verdicts, 8 deterministic guards and 2 substring fallbacks. The draft states 117, 9 and 2. The figure 9 is the post-adjudication guard count (post: 126, 9, 2 = 137), so the draft mixes pre- and post-adjudication counts. It was inherited from the revision-0 report, which I disagree with here.')
    L.append('2. **Reply parser of the substitute runs is undisclosed (WEAKER, CC2-D-04, CC2-MGP-46, CC2-ABS-11, CC2-DIS-09).** All 6,480 stored actions equal the output of an uncommitted working-tree parser (strict json-fence normalization, file time 2026-10-02T11:00:26Z, one minute before the Gemini medium run). With the parser of the baseline commit, 49 (low), 471 (medium) and 212 (high) replies are invalid; the cell A accuracy of Gemini medium would be 0.406 instead of 0.808 and that of Gemini high 0.478 instead of 0.961. The sign reversal for Gemini high and the 0.961 used in the discussion depend on this. GLM and gpt-oss replies parse identically under both parsers.')
    L.append('3. **Mean indexed position (CONTRADICTED, CC2-MGP-08).** Equality across actions holds in each public split, but 3.575 is the development split only (train 3.600, pooled public 3.5875).')
